\caption(Linear kernel PCA centres the original scalar predictor and reproduces its single nonzero principal component. Raw and centred Gram entries are shown together.)
\alttext(Training scores at zero, one and two and one projected query at three appear beside the first centred-kernel row. Tables show the exact Gram matrices, rank-one spectrum and zero query projection loss.)


>> Four quadratic points make the nonlinear features explicit

Take x = (−2,−1,1,2) and \(k(x,z)=(xz+1)^2\).
An explicit feature map is \(\phi(x)=(x^2,\sqrt2x,1)\), because its dot product
expands to that kernel. The centred features are
\((x^2-2.5,\sqrt2x,0)\). Their two nonzero columns are orthogonal over these four
points, with squared norms 9 and 20. Therefore the leading score is \(\sqrt2x\),
the second is \(x^2-2.5\), and Gram eigenvalues are 20 and 9, up to score signs.
The second component joins opposite signs of x with the same magnitude. This demonstrates
a nonlinear feature without claiming that principal components identify a class boundary.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/kpca_quadratic_four.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame d;d.add_column("x",std::vector<double>{-2,-1,1,2});
  const dm::stats::KernelPCA m(d,{"x"},{.kernel="polynomial",.gamma=1,.degree=2,.coef0=1});
  const std::vector<std::string> magnitude={"outer magnitude","inner magnitude","inner magnitude","outer magnitude"};auto features=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  features.points({-2,-1,1,2},{1.5,-1.5,-1.5,1.5},"x squared - 2.5",{37,99,235},6).title("The centred quadratic feature").x_label("raw x").y_label("x squared - training mean").y_limits(-2.5,3);
  auto scores=m.plot_embedding(magnitude).title("Linear and quadratic score axes").y_limits(-2.5,3);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(features).add(scores).size(1100,490).fit_panels().save_svg("build/kpca_quadratic_four.svg");
  std::print("{}\n\n{}\n",m.spectrum().to_md(6),m.projection_details(d).to_md(6));
}
```
