\caption(A polynomial kernel reproduces a hand-written finite feature map. Two retained axes span its complete centred training feature space.)
\alttext(The centred squared predictor is plotted against x, then the two kernel scores are coloured by inner or outer magnitude. The spectrum has eigenvalues twenty and nine and the training projection losses vanish to roundoff.)


>> Three Gaussian points give two exact eigenvalues

For x = (−1,0,1), write \(a=e^{-\gamma}\), \(b=e^{-4\gamma}\).
The uncentred kernel rows are (1,a,b), (a,1,a), (b,a,1).
Reflection symmetry produces the odd unit vector \((-1,0,1)/\sqrt2\) and the even
unit vector \((1,-2,1)/\sqrt6\), both orthogonal to the constant direction.
Their centred eigenvalues are
\(\lambda_{odd}=1-b\) and \(\lambda_{even}=1-4a/3+b/3\).
At gamma one, both are positive; retaining both recovers all centred feature energy
of these three observations, without recovering a general raw-space inverse map.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/kpca_rbf_three.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame d;d.add_column("x",std::vector<double>{-1,0,1});const dm::stats::KernelPCA m(d,{"x"},{.gamma=1});
  auto axes=dm::graphics::RPlot::create(),geometry=m.plot_embedding().title("Two feature-space coordinates");axes.points({-1,0,1},m.dimension(0),"odd axis",{37,99,235},6).points({-1,0,1},m.dimension(1),"even axis",{220,38,38},6).title("Three-point odd and even modes").x_label("raw x").y_label("score").y_limits(-1.2,1.3);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(axes).add(geometry).size(1100,490).fit_panels().save_svg("build/kpca_rbf_three.svg");
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame reference;reference.add_column("mode",std::vector<std::string>{"odd","even"});reference.add_column("closed_form",std::vector<double>{1-std::exp(-4.),1-4*std::exp(-1.)/3+std::exp(-4.)/3});reference.add_column("computed",m.eigenvalues());std::print("{}\n\n{}\n",reference.to_md(9),m.diagnostics().to_md(9));
}
```
