\alttext(Two embeddings of four inner and four outer axis-aligned points are coloured by ring. Small gamma preserves an angular two-axis pattern; at gamma point three the leading coordinate separates ring radii. Tables list the input and leading spectra.)


> Iris measurements

>> Raw-centimetre kernels and the linear-PCA identity

`dm::datasets::iris()` contains 150 complete observations, four numeric measurements in
centimetres and 50 flowers in each of three species. All four measurements enter the
kernel; Species is reserved for descriptive colouring and the later split. No fitted
classifier or species-based gamma selection is part of this analysis.

The linear kernel must reproduce centred, unscaled PCA: its Gram eigenvalues are n−1
times sample covariance eigenvalues, and scores agree up to signs or repeated-subspace
rotations. The program compares two-component score Gram matrices, avoiding sign choices.
The RBF gamma values 0.13 and 10 are prespecified illustrations in the raw-centimetre
metric, not claims of optimality. The polynomial kernel's explicit example already showed
what its nonlinear map does; a label-ranked comparison of arbitrary kernels would add a
supervised choice to an unsupervised illustration.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/kpca_iris_maps.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  const auto d=dm::datasets::iris();const std::vector<std::string> f={"Sepal.Length","Sepal.Width","Petal.Length","Petal.Width"};const auto labels=d.get_column<std::string>("Species").values();
  const dm::stats::PCA pca(d,f,{.center=true,.scale=false});const dm::stats::KernelPCA linear(d,f,{.kernel="linear"}),rbf(d,f,{.gamma=.13}),narrow(d,f,{.gamma=10});
  const auto pc=dm::linalg::DenseMatrix<double>::from_columns({pca.component_scores(0),pca.component_scores(1)});const auto difference=linear.embedding()*linear.embedding().transpose()-pc*pc.transpose();
  auto a=pca.plot_scores(labels).title("Centred unscaled PCA").y_limits(-1.6,2.1),b=linear.plot_embedding(labels).title("Linear kernel: the same score geometry").y_limits(-1.6,2.1),c=rbf.plot_embedding(labels).title("RBF gamma 0.13, raw centimetres").y_limits(-.65,1.05),e=narrow.plot_embedding(labels).title("RBF gamma 10, raw centimetres").y_limits(-.6,1.0);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");dm::graphics::RLayout::create(2,2).add(a).add(b).add(c).add(e).size(1100,960).fit_panels().save_svg("build/kpca_iris_maps.svg");
  const auto summary=d|dm::group_by("Species")|dm::summarise(dm::agg::n("n"),dm::agg::mean("Petal.Length","mean_petal_length_cm"),dm::agg::mean("Petal.Width","mean_petal_width_cm"));dm::dstruct::DataFrame check;check.add_column("component",std::vector<double>{1,2});check.add_column("linear_gram_eigenvalue",linear.eigenvalues());check.add_column("pca_variance_times_149",std::vector<double>{149*pca.explained_variance()[0],149*pca.explained_variance()[1]});
  std::print("{} rows, {} columns. Score-Gram Frobenius difference: {:.3e}\n\n{}\n\n{}\n\nRBF .13:\n\n{}\n",d.nrows(),d.ncols(),difference.norm_frobenius(),summary|dm::to_md(3),check.to_md(6),rbf.diagnostics().select({"rank","trace","retained_share","mean_residual_energy"}).to_md(6));
}
```
