\caption(Linear kernel PCA and ordinary unscaled PCA recover the same two-component score geometry. Nonlinear kernels change the geometry before reduction; species colours are external descriptions.)
\alttext(Four panels compare ordinary PCA, linear kernel PCA and Gaussian kernels at gamma point thirteen and ten. Tables give species summaries, the eigenvalue normalization identity and feature-space diagnostics.)


The linear score-Gram discrepancy is 1.494e-12, with leading Gram eigenvalues
630.008014 and 36.157941, matching 149 times the PCA variances. At RBF gamma 0.13,
two components retain 83.45% of this kernel's resolved feature energy, with mean
training projection loss 0.081965. This fraction describes that feature geometry.

>> Gamma sensitivity without using species to select it

We scan declared values in the same raw-unit metric and report retained feature energy,
mean projection loss and original-neighbourhood trustworthiness/continuity at k=10.
Trustworthiness penalizes new false neighbours and continuity penalizes torn original
neighbours. Both use original raw-feature distances as their reference, which is one
chosen criterion, not every possible downstream purpose. This scan describes sensitivity;
it does not select a winner or evaluate a supervised task. Feature-energy shares compare
how much each kernel's own geometry compresses, rather than a common amount of original
measurement variance.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/kpca_iris_gamma.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  const auto d=dm::datasets::iris();const std::vector<std::string> f={"Sepal.Length","Sepal.Width","Petal.Length","Petal.Width"};dm::dstruct::DataFrame results;std::vector<double> x,energy,trust,continuity;
  for(double g:{.0001,.001,.01,.05,.13,.5,2.,10.,100.}){const dm::stats::KernelPCA m(d,f,{.gamma=g});auto row=m.diagnostics();const double t=dm::stats::trustworthiness(d,f,m.embedding(),10),c=dm::stats::continuity(d,f,m.embedding(),10);row.add_column("gamma",std::vector<double>{g});row.add_column("trustworthiness",std::vector<double>{t});row.add_column("continuity",std::vector<double>{c});results=results.nrows()?results.concat_rows(row):row;x.push_back(std::log10(g));energy.push_back(row.double_at("retained_share",0));trust.push_back(t);continuity.push_back(c);}
  auto a=dm::graphics::RPlot::create(),b=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();a.lines(x,energy,"two-axis share",{37,99,235}).title("Compression of each kernel's geometry").x_label("log10 gamma").y_label("retained feature energy").y_limits(0,1.3);b.lines(x,trust,"trustworthiness",{37,99,235}).lines(x,continuity,"continuity",{220,38,38}).title("Raw-metric neighbourhood checks, k = 10").x_label("log10 gamma").y_label("rank preservation").y_limits(0,1.3);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(a).add(b).size(1100,490).fit_panels().save_svg("build/kpca_iris_gamma.svg");
  std::print("{}\n",results.select({"gamma","rank","trace","retained_share","mean_residual_energy","trustworthiness","continuity"}).to_md(6));
}
```
